/*!
\mainpage StBFChain — STAR Big Full Chain Controller

\section overview Overview

\c StBFChain is the central controller for STAR's <b>Big Full Chain</b> (BFC)
reconstruction and simulation workflows.  A user selects the desired processing
steps by providing a comma- or space-separated string of option keys:

\code{.cpp}
StBFChain *chain = new StBFChain("bfc");
chain->Setup();
chain->SetFlags("P2014a,btof,BEmcChkStat,Corr4,OSpaceZ2,OGridLeak3D");
chain->Set_IO_Files(inputFile, outputFile);
chain->Load();
chain->Instantiate();
chain->Init();
while (chain->Make() == kStOk) {}
chain->Finish();
\endcode

\c StBFChain translates this string into a set of \c Bfc_st entries from the
\c BigFullChain.h option table, resolves all transitive dependencies, loads the
required shared libraries, instantiates the maker objects, and configures each
maker via \c SetAttr calls.

\section bfc_struct Option Table Structure

Every BFC option is represented by a \c Bfc_st row (defined in \c Bfc.h):

| Field  | Max length | Purpose |
|--------|-----------|---------|
| \c Key | 63 | User-facing nick name; case-insensitive lookup via \c kOpt() |
| \c Name | 63 | Maker instance name |
| \c Chain | 63 | Parent sub-chain; empty = top chain |
| \c Opts | 255 | Comma-separated dependencies (prefix \c - disables) |
| \c Maker | 63 | C++ class to instantiate; empty = alias only |
| \c Libs | 255 | Shared libraries to load |
| \c Comment | 255 | Description / option value storage |
| \c Flag | 1 | Runtime on/off |

The full table (~1,062 entries in 16 sections) is defined in
<tt>BigFullChain.h</tt>.  An auto-generated Markdown reference is in
<tt>doc/bfc_options_table.md</tt>; regenerate it with:

\code{.sh}
python3 tests/unit/StBFChain/generate_options_table.py
\endcode

\section dep_resolution Dependency Resolution

The option activation pipeline is:

\code
SetFlags("optA optB -optC")
  → SetOptions("optA optB -optC", "Chain")
      → SetOption(+k_A)   // enable optA and its dependencies (recursive)
      → SetOption(+k_B)   // enable optB and its dependencies
      → SetOption(-k_C)   // disable optC only (no recursion)
\endcode

\c SetOption(k) for a positive \a k first calls \c SetOptions(fBFC[k].Opts)
(depth-first expansion of dependencies), then sets \c fBFC[k].Flag = \c kTRUE.
For a negative \a k it only clears \c fBFC[-k].Flag; no dependency expansion
is performed on disable.

\c kOpt() does a case-insensitive linear scan matching \a tag against both the
\c Key and \c Maker fields of every entry.  Timestamp options matching
<tt>sdt|dbv YYYYMMDD[.HHMMSS]</tt> are handled dynamically without a static
table entry.

\section seealso See Also

- \c StBFChain — main class documentation
- \c StBFChainOpt — \c StChainOpt adapter
- <a href="README.md">doc/README.md</a> — full narrative documentation
  including all \c SetAttr tables
- <a href="bfc_options_table.md">doc/bfc_options_table.md</a> — complete BFC
  options reference table
*/
